# std/ci-status (design/stack-publish.md, "ci-status"): an ordinary worker
# (design/tool-contract.md). It holds no token: it reads GitHub through its
# neighbour `DEEP-DEPS/github`, which the github-token is granted to, so that
# one grant covers it. Being a worker, a change to it runs from a copy of caos.
HELP=<<END
What CI says about a branch on GitHub. The first line is the verdict: passing, pending (something has not finished), FAILING (something failed; neutral and skipped checks pass), or no checks. Then every check run and commit status on its head, one per line with its state and link, the failing ones first. With wait-min it waits, reading again every 15 seconds, until something fails or nothing is pending, for at most that many minutes; use start and result to wait in the background. `root` is the stack directory, such as sources/repo: the repository comes from its 00-base.source.json unless given, and branch may be a layer's name (02-tests) or its name without the number, which means that layer's branch (with branch-prefix in front). Without a stack, pass root=. and repository.
@param branch The branch, commit, or layer to read.
@param [repository] HTTPS repository URL on github.com, without credentials. Required when root is not a stack.
@param [branch-prefix] Text put before a layer's branch name, the same value given to stack-publish.
@param [wait-min] Minutes to wait for CI to settle: it returns as soon as a check fails or none is pending, and after that long says it is still pending. Default 0, read once.
@root
@request-id
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/go --worker1:@=worker.go --github:@=DEEP-DEPS/github --help=$HELP
